<item><title>Kon to challenge South Sudan election timetable in court on Monday</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/kon-to-challenge-south-sudan-election-timetable-in-court-on-6ab4b3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/kon-to-challenge-south-sudan-election-timetable-in-court-on-6ab4b3/</guid><category>South Sudan</category><description>The presidential aspirant wants judges to overturn a delay that moved the vote from Dec. 22, 2026, to Feb. 11, 2027.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:39:34 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" length="35634" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>South Sudan backs 200,000-tonne food reserve as millions go hungry</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/south-sudan-backs-200-000-tonne-food-reserve-as-millions-go-2f3cf2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/south-sudan-backs-200-000-tonne-food-reserve-as-millions-go-2f3cf2/</guid><category>South Sudan</category><description>The Council of Ministers has cleared a 200,000-metric-tonne stockpile as food insecurity spreads across the country.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:58:09 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/south-sudan-backs-200-000-tonne-food-reserve-as-millions-go-2f3cf2/share.jpg" length="40888" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/south-sudan-backs-200-000-tonne-food-reserve-as-millions-go-2f3cf2/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>South Sudan launches 2026 malaria survey after child prevalence reaches 52.6%</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/south-sudan-launches-2026-malaria-survey-after-child-22a888/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/south-sudan-launches-2026-malaria-survey-after-child-22a888/</guid><category>South Sudan</category><description>A survey found malaria prevalence among children under five rose from 25% in 2009 to 52.6% in 2023, according to officials.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:43:28 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" length="35634" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Kiir registers to vote as South Sudan prepares for February polls</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/kiir-registers-to-vote-as-south-sudan-prepares-for-february-1dca5d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ss/kiir-registers-to-vote-as-south-sudan-prepares-for-february-1dca5d/</guid><category>South Sudan</category><description>The president received his voter card six days after nationwide registration began, with the exercise scheduled to close on November 28.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:22:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" length="35634" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ss.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
